  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/he-p/4020",
  "definition": "Determination of External Dose from Airborne Radioactive Material",
  "effectiveDate": "2024-07-23",
  "historyNote": "#5903, eff 2-1-95; ss by #6827, eff 8-6-98; ss by #8481, eff 11-5-05; ss by #10604, eff 5-23-14; ss by #14028, eff 7-23-24",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "He-P 4020.07",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p4001-4022.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-P 4020.07 Determination of External Dose from Airborne Radioactive Material",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 4020.07 Determination of External Dose from Airborne Radioactive Material.\n\n(a) Licensees or registrants shall, when determining the dose from airborne radioactive material, include the contribution to the deep-dose equivalent, lens dose equivalent, and shallow-dose equivalent from external exposure to the radioactive cloud.\n\n(b) Airborne radioactivity measurements and DAC values shall not be used as the primary means to assess the deep-dose equivalent when the airborne radioactive material includes radionuclides other than noble gases or if the cloud of airborne radioactive material is not relatively uniform.\n\n(c) The determination of the deep-dose equivalent to an individual shall be based upon measurements using instruments or individual monitoring devices.\n\nSource. #5903, eff 2-1-95; ss by #6827, eff 8-6-98; ss by #8481, eff 11-5-05; ss by #10604, eff 5-23-14; ss by #14028, eff 7-23-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p4001-4022.html"
